### Rate Limit demo — spring-boot-rating-limit
# Run the app, then click the ▶ (Run) gutter icon next to a request.
# This project limits how many calls you can make. Fire the GET below
# repeatedly (fast) and watch it switch from 200 OK -> 429 Too Many Requests.
#
# Watch the response headers:
#   X-Rate-Limit-Remaining          (on 200) tokens left in the bucket
#   X-Rate-Limit-Retry-After-Seconds (on 429) seconds until the bucket refills

@host = http://localhost:8080

### Get all posts (allowed while tokens remain in the bucket)
GET {{host}}/api/posts

### Spam it — run this several times quickly to trigger the rate limit
# Expected: 200 OK a few times (5 for GOLD), then 429 once the bucket is empty.
GET {{host}}/api/posts

### View the seeded data in the H2 console (open in a browser)
# URL:      http://localhost:8080/h2-console
# JDBC URL: jdbc:h2:mem:postsdb   (user: sa, no password)
